      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "bherbruck",
        "email": "brennen.herbruck@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T00:22:02Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): a refusal on the status strip is drawn as an alert\n\nWhen the status line carries a refusal - a command refused through the\nfeedback path, a dark cell's \"cannot ...\" note, or one of the shell's\nrefusal phrasings - the strip draws it in the error ink, bold, behind a\n\"!\" marker on an error-tinted band, until the next status replaces it.\nOrdinary status text stays dim.\n\nFixes #192\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
