      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "bherbruck",
        "email": "brennen.herbruck@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-08T00:57:45Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): routine status reads in the body ink; \"not created\" is a refusal\n\nThe status strip drew routine messages in egui's dim \"weak\" grey,\nnear-invisible on the dark strip (#215). They now use the theme's body\ntext ink, pinned against the strip fill by the body-text contrast gate\nin both built-in themes. \"not created:\" joins the refusal phrasings so\nan operation-create refusal is an alert on any path. Shell snapshots\nmove by the brighter status line.\n\nFixes #215\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
